{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"items\":[{\"id\":\"bao_shuowen_seal\",\"caption\":\"In this small-seal-style redraw, a curved inner form sits within a larger enclosing outline. Shuowen interpreted the arrangement as an unborn child within a pregnant figure; this received-form reading does not establish the graph’s earliest origin.\",\"alt\":\"A curved black form inside a larger enclosing outline, with a short upright stroke above and a long stroke descending from the outline.\",\"selection_reason\":\"The inner-and-outer arrangement makes the traditional Shuowen interpretation visible while keeping it distinct from the unresolved account of the graph’s earliest origin.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"ref003\",\"ref061\",\"ref078\"],\"period\":\"Shuowen small-seal style; modern redraw, not a dated specimen\"}],\"limitations\":[{\"text\":\"The earliest form of 包 remains unresolved. Shuowen’s pregnancy interpretation and the proposal that 包 developed from a graph depicting someone holding a child are competing accounts; this redraw does not establish an ancient form sequence.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"ref014\",\"ref015\",\"ref028\",\"ref061\",\"ref078\"]},{\"text\":\"The historical relationship between Shuowen’s pregnancy interpretation and the transmitted wrapping use has not been established.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"ref054\",\"ref058\",\"ref059\",\"ref061\"]}]}"}}
